WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.647
- I am not registered to vote.

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:02.722
- I am registered to vote

00:00:02.722 --> 00:00:05.982
but I probably will not be
voting this upcoming election.

00:00:05.982 --> 00:00:08.815
(patriotic music)

00:00:10.337 --> 00:00:12.884
- The whole process is
intimidating and confusing

00:00:12.884 --> 00:00:14.846
and I just don't really
know where to begin.

00:00:14.846 --> 00:00:16.626
- I don't think my vote's
going to make a difference.

00:00:16.626 --> 00:00:18.220
The candidates that we've had here,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.119
I haven't been passionate
about any of them.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.138
- It's very time consuming.

00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:24.237
There is a huge line.

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:26.987
(dramatic music)

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:31.851
Oh wow!

00:00:31.851 --> 00:00:33.134
Okay, metal detectors.

00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:35.215
- There's serious security at this.

00:00:35.215 --> 00:00:36.901
There's like a man with a machine gun

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.211
- Dip your hand in purple ink

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:41.392
and you pretty much vote
with your fingerprint

00:00:41.392 --> 00:00:42.894
- People are threatening these women,

00:00:42.894 --> 00:00:44.110
saying if they vote,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.865
they're going to come to their houses

00:00:45.865 --> 00:00:46.906
and attack them.

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:49.999
- Risking your life to go vote

00:00:49.999 --> 00:00:51.862
I mean, it's pretty brave.

00:00:51.862 --> 00:00:53.421
- The ink that they get on their finger,

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:55.354
that's not just like an I voted sticker

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.529
that you can take off.

00:00:56.529 --> 00:00:58.862
It's gonna be there for
the rest of the day.

00:00:58.862 --> 00:01:00.419
So it makes them a target for people

00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:03.097
who are trying to harm them
and that's really scary.

00:01:03.097 --> 00:01:04.715
- I had no idea it was so dangerous

00:01:04.715 --> 00:01:06.903
to do something this simple

00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:09.486
(gentle music)

00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:12.384
(gasp)

00:01:12.384 --> 00:01:14.475
- It's so exciting to see a lot of people

00:01:14.475 --> 00:01:18.250
show up to vote who
fought so hard to do so.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.211
- They were talking about the numbers of

00:01:20.211 --> 00:01:21.680
how many African Americans versus

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.264
how many white people had
gone to the polls to vote

00:01:24.264 --> 00:01:27.295
and they said 80% of
the people in that area

00:01:27.295 --> 00:01:29.243
had gone who were African American

00:01:29.243 --> 00:01:31.731
so that is incredible considering how

00:01:31.731 --> 00:01:34.032
there's so many of us today who say

00:01:34.032 --> 00:01:35.607
I'm not voting.

00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:38.440
(inspiring music)

00:01:40.627 --> 00:01:41.460
- Wow.

00:01:42.747 --> 00:01:44.610
- Some of the men talking
in this, oh my God.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.827
So these women aren't
allowed to leave the house

00:01:47.827 --> 00:01:49.342
without a male chaperone.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.345
Oh well if she leaves the house to go vote

00:01:51.345 --> 00:01:53.696
who's going to take care of the children?

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:55.065
How long is it going to take
for her to leave the house

00:01:55.065 --> 00:01:56.209
and go vote?

00:01:56.209 --> 00:01:57.305
(lips smack) Sit down.

00:01:57.305 --> 00:01:58.214
- At least they're standing up

00:01:58.214 --> 00:02:00.081
for something that they believe in.

00:02:00.081 --> 00:02:02.033
- These women are still
going out and voting

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:04.631
even though there's still
so many borders in their way

00:02:04.631 --> 00:02:06.421
There's not really a border in my way.

00:02:06.421 --> 00:02:07.588
I'm just lazy.

00:02:08.543 --> 00:02:11.126
(gentle music)

00:02:12.792 --> 00:02:14.942
- She's talking about Saving Private Ryan.

00:02:14.942 --> 00:02:17.630
- And how, in China, people
found it kind of strange

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.425
the notion of saving one person

00:02:20.425 --> 00:02:22.993
by risking the lives of six other people.

00:02:22.993 --> 00:02:24.264
She relates that to voting.

00:02:24.264 --> 00:02:27.388
So, kind of saying that
your vote doesn't matter

00:02:27.388 --> 00:02:29.163
it's almost saying that, you know,

00:02:29.163 --> 00:02:30.964
one life doesn't really matter.

00:02:30.964 --> 00:02:33.227
- Me being Cuban and, you know, my parents

00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:36.312
are from a communist country,
voting is not a thing.

00:02:36.312 --> 00:02:39.513
- This World War II veteran
had never missed voting

00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:42.013
and on his deathbed, he votes.

00:02:44.175 --> 00:02:47.519
Yeah, okay, way to make me feel bad.

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:48.898
(upbeat music)

00:02:48.898 --> 00:02:50.976
Watching these videos
kind of made me realize

00:02:50.976 --> 00:02:53.925
the contrast between
how I feel about voting

00:02:53.925 --> 00:02:58.300
and how a lot of other
people feel about voting.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.741
- I feel like the voting
process in America

00:02:59.741 --> 00:03:01.319
is actually pretty simple.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:03.195
- Vote because you have the right to.

00:03:03.195 --> 00:03:05.783
Vote because you feel like
it's your civil liberty to

00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:08.923
and vote because it's
the right thing to do.

00:03:08.923 --> 00:03:10.164
- It's really opened my mind.

00:03:10.164 --> 00:03:11.844
It makes me feel like an (bleep). (laughs)

00:03:11.844 --> 00:03:14.177
- I got some thinking to do.

00:03:15.644 --> 00:03:18.561
- Yeah, I want to register to vote.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.411
Yeah (laughs)

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:25.078
Let me get my email.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:34.382
(laptop shuts)

00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:35.940
That was (bleep) easy. (laughs)

